      "title": "Rclnodejs 2.3.0: ROS 2 Actions over WebSocket and HTTP/SSE",
      "link": "https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/rclnodejs-2-3-0-ros-2-actions-over-websocket-and-http-sse/58817",
      "summary": "Send a goal, follow the feedback, get the result. rclnodejs 2.3.0 , the ROS 2 client library for Node.js, brings ROS 2 actions to web apps over WebSocket and HTTP/SSE. ROS 2 Actions from the Browser The browser SDK derives TypeScript goal, feedback and result types from generated ROS declarations. OpenAPI export also includes action schemas. With an HTTP runtime on port 9001 exposing a running Fibonacci action server as /fibonacci : import { connect } from 'rclnodejs/web'; const ros = await connect({ http: 'http://localhost:9001' }); try { const goal = await ros.action( '/fibonacci', { order: 5 }, { onFeedback: (feedback) => console.log(feedback.sequence) } ); console.log(await goal.result, goal.status); } finally { await ros.close(); } Web capabilities at a glance Together with the topic and service support from earlier releases, actions round out the following client-facing operations, controlled by the same capability allow-list: ROS 2 operation WebSocket HTTP / SSE Publish topic messages Yes HTTP POST Subscribe to topics Yes HTTP GET + SSE (opt-in) Call services Yes HTTP POST Send action goals, receive feedback/results (new) Yes HTTP POST + SSE Request cancellation of an action",
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-13T07:43:15+00:00",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-13T07:43:15+00:00",
      "source": "ROS2 Discourse",
      "section_hint": "로보틱스",
      "articleText": "Rclnodejs 2.3.0: ROS 2 Actions over WebSocket and HTTP/SSE - ROS General - Open Robotics Discourse Rclnodejs 2.3.0: ROS 2 Actions over WebSocket and HTTP/SSE ROS ROS General ros2 , robotwebtools , nodejs , rclnodejs , typescript minggangw October 13, 2026, 7:43am 1 Send a goal, follow the feedback, get the result. rclnodejs 2.3.0 , the ROS 2 client library for Node.js, brings ROS 2 actions to web apps over WebSocket and HTTP/SSE. ROS 2 Actions from the Browser The browser SDK derives TypeScript goal, feedback and result types from generated ROS declarations. OpenAPI export also includes action schemas. With an HTTP runtime on port 9001 exposing a running Fibonacci action server as /fibonacci : import { connect } from 'rclnodejs/web'; const ros = await connect({ http: 'http://localhost:9001' }); try { const goal = await ros.action( '/fibonacci', { order: 5 }, { onFeedback: (feedback) => console.log(feedback.sequence) } ); console.log(await goal.result, goal.status); } finally { await ros.close(); } Web capabilities at a glance Together with the topic and service support from earlier releases, actions round out the following client-facing operations, controlled by the same capability allow-list: ROS 2 operation WebSocket HTTP / SSE Publish topic messages Yes HTTP POST Subscribe to topics Yes HTTP GET + SSE (opt-in) Call services Yes HTTP POST Send action goals, receive feedback/results (new) Yes HTTP POST + SSE Request cancellation of an action goal (new) Yes; server may reject Not supported Try the JavaScript and TypeScript demos for runnable examples. For background on the typed Web SDK and capability runtime first introduced in 2.0.0, see our original announcement . 2 Likes Related topics Topic Replies Views Activity Rclnodejs 2.0.0 — typed Web SDK for ROS 2, ready for Lyrical ROS General ros2 , web , robotwebtools , nodejs , rclnodejs 1 476 June 11, 2026 ROS2 Node.js client with Action support ROS General 1 5083 June 11, 2020 Rclnodejs 2.1: Native ESM for a Web-Native ROS 2 SDK ROS General ros2 , robotwebtools , nodejs , rclnodejs , esm 3 1331 August 18, 2026 Rclnodejs 2.0.0 beta — ROS 2 Lyrical (beta) and Node.js 26 support ROS General web , lyrical , nodejs , rclnodejs , client 0 210 May 6, 2026 Call for contributions: ROS 2 Node.js client ROS General 4 1204 July 17, 2019",
